WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — interface-economics (45s) Narrator Edwin

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:07.579
First, single handoff failures carry exact price tags, like losing a Mars mission over mismatched units.

2
00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:15.888
Second, giant national software-failure numbers come from broad surveys and models, never counting handoffs alone.

3
00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:23.290
Third, checking what each side assumes is cheap, but one team pays while everyone else benefits.

4
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:31.342
On the Mars Climate Orbiter, one team sent thruster data in pound-force seconds while navigation read newton-seconds.

5
00:00:31.342 --> 00:00:39.864
Each program worked on its own, yet an unwritten handoff assumption cost a three-hundred-twenty-eight-million-dollar space project.

6
00:00:40.304 --> 00:00:44.678
Because AI generated code crosses these exact same seams even faster,

7
00:00:44.678 --> 00:00:51.524
embedding units and ranges into machine-checked contracts makes closing handoffs cheaper than skipping them.
